{"schemaVersion":1,"id":"reference:6f1714f84e78025e","name":"MSE-6 Repair Droid","source":{"id":"source:reference-6f1714f84e78025e","title":"MSE-6 Repair Droid","revision":25618,"timestamp":"2024-11-29T02:44:57Z","sha256":"614c16718ef4301427868cf4cc0d60acfd7c9809386bbba2c9aba087b22632f7","url":"https://swse.miraheze.org/w/index.php?oldid=25618","history":"https://swse.miraheze.org/w/index.php?title=MSE-6%20Repair%20Droid&action=history"},"article":{"sourceId":"source:reference-6f1714f84e78025e","blocks":[{"tag":"p","children":[{"tag":"i","children":["Reference Book: ",{"tag":"a","children":["Force Unleashed Campaign Guide"],"href":"https://swse.miraheze.org/wiki/Force_Unleashed_Campaign_Guide"}]},"\n"]},{"tag":"p","children":[{"tag":"i","children":["Affiliations: ",{"tag":"a","children":["The Galactic Empire"],"href":"https://swse.miraheze.org/wiki/The_Galactic_Empire","referenceId":"reference:f9c9a48674cc3415"}]},"\n"]},{"tag":"p","children":["The MSE-6, or \"Mouse Droid,\" is a wheeled Droid used for basic tasks such as maintenance of a single mechanical system, message delivery, cleaning, and even testing dangerous areas of a damaged ",{"tag":"a","children":["Starship"],"href":"https://swse.miraheze.org/wiki/Starship"}," or station to make sure it is safe for living creatures (and more expensive Droids). The MSE-6 is the result of a long line of small, dedicated, cheap Droids used by the Republic and other governments. The MSE-6, however, is almost exclusively in use by the Empire, which bought nearly the whole run (at a steep discount). The Droids are used for Imperial installations that have high crew requirements, such as ",{"tag":"a","children":["Star Destroyers"],"href":"https://swse.miraheze.org/wiki/Star_Destroyers"},", to cut down on the need for larger Droids and ",{"tag":"a","children":["Human"],"href":"https://swse.miraheze.org/wiki/Human","referenceId":"reference:9ffa865f2bc6e850"}," work crews as much as possible.\n"]},{"tag":"p","children":["An MSE-6 is generally given a single specific task and the needed gear to accomplish it (generally small tools it can keep in its interior storage space). Though an MSE-6 looks like a small black box on wheels, it has two folding arms it can use for basic tasks. Although they are dedicated and loyal, MSE-6 Droids suffer from an overdeveloped threat assessment program. They are skittish, and they frequently flee from anything new or frightening. Any time an MSE-6 moves -1 step down its ",{"tag":"a","children":["Condition Track"],"href":"https://swse.miraheze.org/wiki/Condition_Track"}," as the result of an ability that targeted its ",{"tag":"a","children":["Will Defense"],"href":"https://swse.miraheze.org/wiki/Will_Defense"},", the Droid immediately flees for 1d6 minutes.\n"]},{"tag":"p","children":["MSE-6 Repair Droids can't be played as ",{"tag":"a","children":["Droid Heroes"],"href":"https://swse.miraheze.org/wiki/Droid_Heroes"},".\n"]},"\n",{"tag":"h2","children":["MSE-6 Repair Droid Statistics (CL 0)"]},"\n",{"tag":"h4","children":["Normal"]},"\n",{"tag":"p","children":["Tiny ",{"tag":"a","children":["5th-Degree Droid"],"href":"https://swse.miraheze.org/wiki/5th-Degree_Droid"}," ",{"tag":"a","children":["Nonheroic"],"href":"https://swse.miraheze.org/wiki/Nonheroic","referenceId":"reference:1bca2ef1d9ebe1c3"}," 2\n"]},{"tag":"p","children":[{"tag":"b","children":[{"tag":"a","children":["Initiative"],"href":"https://swse.miraheze.org/wiki/Initiative","referenceId":"reference:3e687de48a6ad4e5"},":"]}," +3; ",{"tag":"b","children":["Senses:"]}," ",{"tag":"a","children":["Darkvision"],"href":"https://swse.miraheze.org/wiki/Darkvision"},", ",{"tag":"a","children":["Perception"],"href":"https://swse.miraheze.org/wiki/Perception","referenceId":"reference:bd18e320a6bb9f53"}," +6\n"]},{"tag":"p","children":[{"tag":"b","children":["Languages:"]}," Basic (understand only), ",{"tag":"a","children":["Binary"],"href":"https://swse.miraheze.org/wiki/Binary","referenceId":"reference:ee